{"arena": "Z", "t": 1792893761.0, "seq": 42, "op": "mutate", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "cost": 0.00059254, "parents": ["Z11"], "log": {"edges": [["progress", "goal_field", "call"]], "n_edges": 1, "editable": ["s3", "s4"], "llm": {"in": 467, "out": 983, "cache_read": 5434, "cache_write": 0, "seconds": 9.0, "stop": "end_turn"}, "reply": "This mutation makes `goal_field` route around enemies when the bot is hurt and enemy champions are visible. Otherwise it returns the cached per-turn field, so the common path stays cheap. I have not run it, so the fuel cost of the `field_avoid` call in fights is untested.\n\n```python\n@gene('s3', 'distance field to the goals; when hurt with enemy champions in view, re-route around enemy tiles (else cached per-turn field)', parents=['s3'])\ndef goal_field() -> Field:\n    if me().health_frac < 0.5 and count(1 for u in enemies() if u.is_champion) > 0:\n        return field_avoid(goals(), walls() | enemy_tiles(), goals())\n    return GOAL_F\n```"}, "error": "GenomeError: goal_field line 58: expected Bool, got Num", "birth": 15, "accepted": false, "fingerprint": null}
