{"arena": "Z", "t": 1792893870.0, "seq": 68, "op": "mutate", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "cost": 0.00092824, "parents": ["Z23"], "log": {"edges": [["progress", "goal_field", "call"]], "n_edges": 1, "editable": ["s3", "s4"], "llm": {"in": 774, "out": 1593, "cache_read": 5434, "cache_write": 0, "seconds": 8.4, "stop": "end_turn"}, "reply": "This mutation makes `goal_field` route around enemy champions and walls instead of returning the plain cached field. It reuses `goals()` as the stop set so the search ends once all goals are reached. The `GOAL_F` keep stays declared but is no longer read.\n\n```python\n@gene(\"s3b\", \"distance field to goals routed around walls and enemy champions (engine field_avoid, stops once goals are reached)\", parents=[\"s3\"])\ndef goal_field() -> Field:\n    return field_avoid(goals(), walls() | enemy_tiles(), goals())\n```\n\nThe trade-off is fuel. This is an engine call that the zero-argument gene recomputes on every pass of the loop, not the once-per-turn cached read that `s3` did. The stop-set bound keeps the search small, but if the fuel budget is tight this could cost tempo, so it's worth checking against the arena results."}, "error": "GenomeError: line 88: gene goal_field redefined or shadows a builtin", "birth": 28, "accepted": false, "fingerprint": null}
